Package: npte
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Simone Basso <bassosimone@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/bassosimone/npte
# Comment lines are stripped by makedeb.bash: binary control files do
# not allow comments, but we want derivations next to the constants.
#
# Policy 3.5 wants dependencies on essential packages (coreutils,
# grep, util-linux) to be versioned. We only use ancient POSIX
# behavior, so the floors are lineage points rather than features,
# except for runuser:
#
# - coreutils 5.0 (2003) is the fileutils/sh-utils/textutils merge,
#   the first release named coreutils; install/env/rm predate it
# - any POSIX grep works (we use -F, -v, --); 2.0 (1993) is the
#   start of the modern GNU grep codebase
# - util-linux 2.23 (2013) is the first version shipping runuser
#
# @LIBC@ is the highest GLIBC_x.y symbol version referenced by the
# npte binary, computed by makedeb.bash at build time.
Depends: bubblewrap, coreutils (>= 5.0), debootstrap, grep (>= 2.0), iproute2, iptables, kmod, libc6 (>= @LIBC@), procps, python3 (>= 3.14), systemd-container, util-linux (>= 2.23), sudo | sudo-rs
Description: Network Performance Testing Environment
 Builds isolated Linux network namespaces wired with veth pairs and
 shaped via tc/netem, to test how a network client behaves on a
 realistic access link without real hardware.
